(Ord. No. 2003-81, § 1, 7-29-03; Ord. No. 2026-32(26-O-1370), § 8, 9-17-26)

2276:
(a) It shall be a violation of this division for an operator to refer a parking penalty invoice to collections, report a parking penalty invoice to a credit reporting agency, add collection fees, or initiate legal action until the customer has been provided written notice and not less than 30 days to dispute the invoice.
(b) Each parking penalty invoice shall provide notice to the customer of the following:
(1) The date, time, and location of the alleged violation;
(2) The vehicle license plate number;
(3) The posted rate applicable at the time of entry;
(4) The rule allegedly violated;
(5) Photographic or digital evidence supporting the invoice;
(6) The amount owed;
(7) The deadline to dispute;
(8) The method to dispute online, by telephone, by email, and by mail;
(9) The name and contact information of the operator and any third-party enforcement or collection vendor; and
(10) Notice that the customer may submit evidence of payment, attempted payment, validation, patronage of a validating tenant, system failure, unclear signage, or other mitigating circumstances.
(c) Every operator shall maintain a dispute resolution process that is accessible online, by telephone, by email, and by mail by which a customer may dispute any parking penalty and where supported by the evidence have the same dismissed by the operator.
(d) The dispute process shall allow a customer to submit documents, screenshots, receipts, validation records, witness statements, photographs, or other evidence.
(e) No operator shall require payment of a disputed parking penalty invoice as a condition of submitting a dispute.
(f) An operator shall acknowledge receipt of a dispute within five business days.
(g) An operator shall provide a written decision on the dispute within 21 business days after receiving the dispute.
(h) The written decision shall state the factual basis for the decision and shall identify the evidence relied upon.
(i) No parking penalty shall be enforced while a timely dispute is pending.
(j) Where an operator determines that a disputed parking penalty invoice was issued in error the operator shall cease enforcement activity and withdraw the parking penalty invoice.
(Ord. No. 2026-32(26-O-1370), § 9, 9-17-26)

